That is what I thought, but I couldn't recreate it with a simple test case outside Stan. For example,

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp$ cat bug.cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <Eigen/Dense>

int main()
{
  Eigen::MatrixXd m(3,3);
  m << 1, 2, 3,
       4, 5, 6,
       7, 8, -9;
  std::cout << "m is " << std::endl << m << std::endl;
  return 0;
}

and then

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/opt/stan$ cppcheck -f -I/usr/include/eigen3 bug.cpp

does not flag anything.

Ben

