It turns out I was calling cppcheck without -I src/ , which caused problems. Here is the correct way

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp$ cppcheck -j 8 -I lib/eigen_3.1.1/ -I lib/eigen_3.1.1/unsupported -I lib/boost_1.51.0/ -I src/ --enable=all --inconclusive --xml --template=gcc --force src/ 2> /tmp/cppcheck.xml

although that excludes rstan/. Then to make the report

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp$ ./cppcheck-htmlreport --title=Stan --file=/tmp/cppcheck.xml --report-dir=/tmp/Stan --source-dir=/opt/stan

So, now the attached has only 7 things.

Ben

