On 11/5/12 8:05 PM, Ben Goodrich wrote:
 > It turns out I was calling cppcheck without -I src/ , which caused problems. Here is the correct way

These are almost all in I/O or things we don't
really use (like thread-safe agrad).  But I
fixed what's there and it should all be OK other
than perhaps what it thinks is a memory leak.

I switched the C-style casts to a C++-style
static_cast<>() in agrad/agrad.hpp.

I initialized the var's vi_ to a null ptr (0) in
agrad_threadsafe.

I don't know what its deal is with memory leaks in
the agrad_threadsafe version.  Its error report is on the
member variable and there's no allocation there.

I removed the throws from the destructors in agrad::chainable.

