I managed to get include-what-you-use working; see

http://code.google.com/p/include-what-you-use/
http://www.llvm.org/devmtg/2010-11/Silverstein-IncludeWhatYouUse.pdf

In short, it is a clang-based tool that passes over the .cpp files and tells you if your #includes are suboptimal. It is mostly a For Google, By Google thing but they released it for other C++ projects. In particular, apparently Google has an internal law that every .cpp file must have a .hpp file with the same basename.

> WARNING: include-what-you-use only analyzes .cc (or .cpp) files built by make, along with their corresponding .h files. If your project has a .h file with no corresponding .cc file, iwyu will ignore it. include-what-you-use supports the AddGlobToReportIWYUViolationsFor() function which can be used to indicate other files to analyze, but it's not currently exposed to the user in any way.

Anyway, here is what it does with the oxford model, for example (They have a python script that is supposed to make all these changes automagically, but I don't totally trust it yet)

oxford.cpp should add these lines:
#include <bits/mathcalls.h>             // for sqrt
#include <stddef.h>                     // for size_t
#include <algorithm>                    // for fill
#include <cmath>                        // for isnan, isfinite, fpclassify
#include <exception>                    // for exception
#include <ios>                          // for operator&
#include <iosfwd>                       // for ostream, stringstream, etc
#include <iostream>                     // for cerr
#include <limits>                       // for numeric_limits
#include <memory>                       // for allocator
#include <new>                          // for operator new
#include <ostream>                      // for operator<<, basic_ostream, etc
#include <sstream>                      // for basic_stringstream
#include <stdexcept>                    // for domain_error, runtime_error
#include <string>                       // for string, operator+, etc
#include <vector>                       // for vector
#include "Eigen/src/Core/Map.h"
#include "Eigen/src/Core/Matrix.h"      // for Matrix
#include "Eigen/src/Core/util/Constants.h"  // for Dynamic
#include "Eigen/src/Core/util/Memory.h"  // for first_aligned
#include "boost/exception/diagnostic_information.hpp"
#include "boost/format/alt_sstream_impl.hpp"
#include "boost/format/format_implementation.hpp"
#include "boost/math/special_functions/fpclassify.hpp"  // for isfinite, etc
#include "boost/optional/optional.hpp"  // for get_pointer
#include "stan/agrad/agrad.hpp"         // for var, operator+, operator<<, etc
#include "stan/agrad/matrix.hpp"        // for assign, initialize_variable
#include "stan/agrad/special_functions.hpp"  // for inv_logit
#include "stan/gm/command.hpp"          // for nuts_command
#include "stan/io/csv_writer.hpp"       // for csv_writer
#include "stan/io/reader.hpp"           // for reader
#include "stan/io/var_context.hpp"      // for var_context
#include "stan/io/writer.hpp"           // for writer
#include "stan/math/error_handling.hpp"  // for check_greater_or_equal
#include "stan/math/matrix.hpp"         // for get_base1, stan_print
#include "stan/math/special_functions.hpp"  // for inv_logit
#include "stan/model/prob_grad_ad.hpp"  // for prob_grad_ad
