It's not really that dangerous, except that it could lead to more
people asking basic questions on the mailing list about the
differences between point estimation and Bayesian inference. Then
again, that's arguably an opportunity to educate, which is arguably a
good thing.

You are correct that it's finite-diffing the auto-diff gradients. I'm
being pretty conservative and using a 4th-order finite difference
formula rather than a tiny perturbation size, so hopefully the
numerical problems won't get too hairy.

I'll wrap up the output format and push. Probably this afternoon.

Matt

